# Page architecture

## One folder per page

Each page lives in its own folder under `src/pages/`:

```
src/pages/
  LibraryPage/
    LibraryPage.tsx        # The page component
    LibraryPage.models.ts  # Types/interfaces used only by this page
    LibraryPage.constants.ts # Constants used only by this page
    LibraryPage.helpers.ts  # Helper functions (component-specific)
  DictionaryPage/
    DictionaryPage.tsx
    DictionaryPage.models.ts
    DictionaryPage.constants.ts
    DictionaryPage.helpers.ts
  ...
```

- **Reusable** types/constants live in `src/types/`, `src/lib/`, or shared constants modules—not duplicated in page folders.
- **Router imports**: Keep importing the page component from the folder, e.g. `@/pages/LibraryPage/LibraryPage` or `@/pages/LibraryPage` (barrel if you add one).

## File roles

- **PageName.tsx**: Only the React component and its local state/hooks. Compose features and shared components; avoid large inline logic.
- **PageName.models.ts**: Types, interfaces, and type-only exports used by this page (and its helpers). Move types out of the `.tsx` file.
- **PageName.constants.ts**: Constants (e.g. options arrays, config) used only by this page. Reusable constants stay in a shared place.
- **PageName.helpers.ts**: Pure or mostly-pure functions and small utilities used only by this page (see helpers-extract rule).

## Reusable UI and features

- **Shared components**: `src/components/common/`, `src/components/layout/`, `src/components/features/`.
- Prefer extracting repeated page sections into components in these folders so pages stay thin and only compose features.
